+Further, applying four-component PCA reduced qubit count, circuit depth, CZ count, and hardware-induced kernel distortion. This resource reduction corresponded to a loss of predictive information in some configurations, with a substantial loss for CLaMP and a smaller loss for MBR. PCA should therefore not be treated solely as a noise-reduction step; its resource benefit must be evaluated against representation loss for each dataset.
 
